Update 2026-11-03: rebased onto the new head of #1279 (one test commit, see its update), and one commit added, 61dddbfa0 "keep the fused SM75 prefill index scores in FP32". The fused Turing scorer of this PR rounded each head product q_h . k to fp16 before the ReLU. The index keys enter without their per-key scale (e4m3 values up to 448), so one product can pass fp16's 65,504, as #1327 describes for main's cuBLAS tile (#1328 fixes that one). The kernel now keeps the FP32 accumulator; registers and shared memory are unchanged, and two conversions per score fall away.

How large this is in a real model: on GLM-5.3-Flash, PP=5 over three Tesla V100 and two Quadro RTX 8000 with our fork's production entry, I counted the prefill index logits that feed the top-k, in the causal window, over prompts up to 516,196 tokens. Non-finite share per stage: 36.9 % and 31.0 % on the two RTX 8000 stages (this scorer), 24.3 %, 3.2 % and 53.8 % on the three V100 stages (the cuBLAS tile); single layers up to 70 %. With all three routes in FP32 (this commit, the Triton scorer of #1282 and the change of #1328), 0.000 % on every stage and every index layer over the same prompts. In an A/B of that fork build against the same build without the three changes (runs T T P T P, T#2 + T#4 against P#3 + P#5), time to first token at 516,196 tokens was 244.01 / 244.20 s against 248.42 / 248.32 s and prefill of 8,687 tokens 4.15 to 4.24 s against 4.21 to 4.30 s (leaving out the first request of P#3, the first boot of the reference build, at 6.00 s); short-prompt answers and GSM8K-30 (29/30) were identical, and one of the two reference runs ran into a repetition loop at 516,196 tokens while no fixed run did. DeepSeek-V4-Flash shows 0 % non-finite scores already without the change (same count, prompts up to 500,000 tokens); its query norms stay far below the overflow.

New test: test_turing_fused_scorer_survives_unscaled_key_magnitudes in tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v4_sm70_indexer.py (keys at the e4m3 maximum with scale 2^-8, two query heads of 2.0 weighted +1 and -1, 32 and 64 heads); it asserts finite scores that match the FP32 reference. The branch now holds 23 commits (the 16 of #1279 and 7 new).

Tests on dff18c253, which is this head without the test commit of #1279 below it, native build, one pytest per file with stock Triton 3.6, a Quadro RTX 8000 / a Tesla V100 as device 0: test_host_reduce.py 3 passed / 3 passed; test_dsv4_sm70_sparse_bmm.py 0 passed, 12 skipped / 12 passed; test_dsv4_sparse_prefill_bmm.py 17 passed / 17 passed; test_paged_prefill_attention_sm75.py 21 passed / 5 passed, 16 skipped; test_skinny_sm70_moe.py 103 passed, 33 skipped / 89 passed, 47 skipped; test_sm70_qpn8_block_fp8.py 113 passed, 10 skipped / 1 failed, 95 passed, 27 skipped; test_compressor_kv_cache.py 32 passed, 6 skipped / 32 passed, 6 skipped; test_deepseek_v4_sm70_indexer.py 33 passed / 30 passed, 3 skipped; test_deepseek_v4_sm70_qnorm_rope_kv_insert.py 4 passed / 4 passed; test_deepseek_v4_sm70_routes.py 30 passed / 30 passed; test_block_fp8_qpn8_capabilities.py 24 passed / 24 passed; test_turing_qpn_kernel_selection.py 34 passed / 34 passed; test_flash_v100_dense_prefill_availability.py 2 passed / 2 passed; test_sparse_indexer_decode_seq_lens.py 11 passed / 11 passed; test_cudagraph_dispatch.py 51 passed / 51 passed; test_gpu_model_runner_v2.py 2 failed, 5 passed / 2 failed, 5 passed; test_prefill_overlap.py 16 passed / 16 passed. The failures are the same on main 4d57473db built from source: in test_gpu_model_runner_v2.py test_sm70_v2_mtp_profile_reports_from_last_pp_stage[pp2-last-stage-tp1] and [pp2-first-stage] on both cards, and test_sm70_qpn8_block_fp8.py::test_volta_medium_prefill_keeps_original_turbomind_output[64] on the V100. On this head, the two files of #1279's test commit: @@FIX_1280@@

pre-commit run --from-ref 4d57473db --to-ref HEAD: every hook passes except check-layering, which reports moe_runner.py (platform coupling 37 -> 39) exactly as main 4d57473db does. pre-commit run mypy-3.10 --all-files --hook-stage manual: no issues apart from three in vllm/v1/attention/backends/flash_v100/runtime.py that come from a local flash_attn_v100 checkout and that main shows the same way.

